{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CftafUmaHwBeH1sTkEMLr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist. I didn't open the dashboard to check that the panels render, and the rule has no connector, so it has no notification action.\n\n**What the data holds:** the Kibana Sample Data Logs view (`kibana_sample_data_logs`) has one document per web request. The fields I used are:\n- `timestamp`, the time field.\n- `response`, the HTTP status code, stored as a string and used through `response.keyword`.\n- `bytes`, the response size.\n- `extension`, the file type requested, used through `extension.keyword`.\n\nIt also has client and geo fields such as `clientip`, `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `host`, `url` and `referer`.\n\n**Dashboard \"EFF-64958fc3 Web logs overview\"** has four panels:\n- Total requests, as a single-number metric.\n- Requests over time, as a line chart.\n- Requests by response code, as a pie chart.\n- Average bytes by extension, as a bar chart.\n\nIt's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-64958fc3-web-logs-overview-ced7608179fb.\n\n**Rule \"EFF-64958fc3 5xx spike\"** (id `7dabde7d-49f6-419c-9f39-4072515bccde`):\n- It's an Elasticsearch query rule that runs every minute over the last 5 minutes.\n- It matches documents where `response.keyword` is `5xx` (regexp `5[0-9][0-9]`) and fires when the count is above 10.\n- It was created disabled, so I enabled it. It's now running."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":975,"cache_read_input_tokens":20299,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":975},"output_tokens":531,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"017ae068-30d4-576d-802e-c9b7